# Content voice & claims

Follow [CONTENT.md](../../CONTENT.md) when editing marketing copy.

## Must

- Keep positioning as **AI-first digital engineering**.
- Pull company facts (contact, legal, default SEO) from `frontend/src/constants/company.ts` — do not duplicate or invent.
- Reuse `@/content/shared` for CTAs (`CTA`, `contactCta`, `consultationCta`, `FINAL_PAIR*`) and `DISCLAIMERS`.
- Annotate page blocks with shared types (`SeoMeta`, `PageHero`, `FinalCta`, `FaqSection`, etc.).

## Must not invent

- Metrics (uptime %, savings, ROI, user counts)
- Testimonials, logos, awards, certifications not held
- Guarantees (“100%”, “always”, “zero downtime”)
- Fake client case-study results, fake jobs, fake blog/resources
- Company size, years of experience, or unapproved locations

## Work / portfolio

Public copy must read as a live site — never “placeholder / demo / when approved” notes in the UI. Portfolio shows projects without disclaimer strips. Do not invent Results, metrics, or fake client outcomes.

## Voice

Clear over clever. Prefer “you” and buyer situations over capability catalogues. Short scannable sections; solution pages: hero → problem → what we build → ≤4 steps → work → FAQ → CTA. Avoid hype and jargon walls.
